{"issues":[{"expand":"renderedFields,names,schema,operations,editmeta,changelog,versionedRepresentations","id":"90271","self":"https://mojira.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/90271","key":"MC-265805","renderedFields":{"summary":null,"issuetype":null,"watches":null,"customfield_10070":null,"customfield_10061":"","created":"13/Oct/23 3:04 AM","customfield_10050":"","customfield_10051":null,"description":"<h3><a name=\"Thebug\"></a>The bug</h3>\n<p>Before 23w41a, tail-recursive functions, which call themselves with <tt>/function</tt> at the end of their body, worked quite efficiently. They consume only a constant amount of memory resources regardless of the depth of the recursion.<br>\nSince 23w41a, however, even tail-recursive functions consume more memory resources for each recursive call.</p>\n\n<h3><a name=\"Howtoreproduce\"></a>How to reproduce</h3>\n<ol>\n\t<li><div class=\"code panel\" style=\"border-width: 1px;\"><div class=\"codeContent panelContent\">\n<pre class=\"code-java\">/gamerule maxCommandChainLength 2147483647</pre>\n</div></div></li>\n\t<li><div class=\"code panel\" style=\"border-width: 1px;\"><div class=\"codeContent panelContent\">\n<pre class=\"code-java\">/function mc-265805:f</pre>\n</div></div>\n<p> → Eventually, the game crashes due to <tt>java.lang.OutOfMemoryError: Java heap space</tt></p></li>\n</ol>\n\n\n<div class=\"panel\" style=\"border-width: 1px;\"><div class=\"panelHeader\" style=\"border-bottom-width: 1px;\"><b>data/mc-265805/functions/f.mcfunction</b></div><div class=\"panelContent\">\n<div class=\"code panel\" style=\"border-width: 1px;\"><div class=\"codeContent panelContent\">\n<pre class=\"code-java\">function mc-265805:f</pre>\n</div></div>\n</div></div>\n\n<h3><a name=\"Codeanalysis\"></a>Code analysis</h3>\n\n<div class=\"panel\" style=\"border-width: 1px;\"><div class=\"panelHeader\" style=\"border-bottom-width: 1px;\"><b>net/minecraft/server/commands/FunctionCommand.java</b></div><div class=\"panelContent\">\n<div class=\"code panel\" style=\"border-width: 1px;\"><div class=\"codeContent panelContent\">\n<pre class=\"code-java\"><span class=\"code-keyword\">public</span> <span class=\"code-keyword\">static</span> &lt;T <span class=\"code-keyword\">extends</span> ExecutionCommandSource&lt;T&gt;&gt; void queueFunctions(\n    Collection&lt;CommandFunction&lt;T&gt;&gt; functions,\n    @Nullable CompoundTag arguments,\n    T sender,\n    T senderForExecution,\n    ExecutionControl&lt;T&gt; control,\n    FunctionCommand.Callbacks&lt;T&gt; callbacks\n) <span class=\"code-keyword\">throws</span> CommandSyntaxException {\n    CommandDispatcher&lt;T&gt; dispatcher = sender.dispatcher();\n    MutableInt accumulatedReturnValue = <span class=\"code-keyword\">new</span> MutableInt();\n\n    <span class=\"code-keyword\">for</span>(CommandFunction&lt;T&gt; function : functions) {\n        ResourceLocation id = function.id();\n\n        <span class=\"code-keyword\">try</span> {\n            T listener = senderForExecution.clearCallbacks().withReturnValueConsumer(returnValue -&gt; {\n                <span class=\"code-object\">int</span> value = accumulatedReturnValue.addAndGet(returnValue);\n                callbacks.signalResult(sender, id, value);\n                sender.storeResults(<span class=\"code-keyword\">true</span>, value);\n            });\n            InstantiatedFunction&lt;T&gt; instantiatedFunction = function.instantiate(arguments, dispatcher, listener);\n            control.queueNext(<span class=\"code-keyword\">new</span> CallFunction&lt;&gt;(instantiatedFunction).bind(listener));\n        } <span class=\"code-keyword\">catch</span> (FunctionInstantiationException e) {\n            <span class=\"code-keyword\">throw</span> ERROR_FUNCTION_INSTANTATION_FAILURE.create(id, e.messageComponent());\n        }\n    }\n}\n</pre>\n</div></div>\n</div></div>\n<p>Because <tt>listener</tt>'s return value consumer captures the original <tt>sender</tt>, JVM cannot release <tt>sender</tt> while <tt>listener</tt> is alive. In the case of recursive calls, a <tt>listener</tt> becomes the <tt>sender</tt> of another function call, chaining to the initial sender. Although calling a tail-recursive function still consumes only a constant amount of the command queue space, it now consumes a linear amount of memory resources due to the chain of execution command sources.</p>\n\n<h3><a name=\"Heapdumpanalysis\"></a>Heap dump analysis</h3>\n\n<p>Using VisualVM and a deobfuscated server.jar of 23w41a, a heap dump was obtained when the heap was almost full. According to the heap dump, the heap was almost fully occupied by the following three objects:</p>\n<ul>\n\t<li><tt>net.minecraft.commands.CommandSourceStack</tt>: <b>30.6%</b></li>\n\t<li><tt>net.minecraft.server.commands.FunctionCommand$$Lambda+0x000001c05ebefc78</tt>: <b>30.6%</b></li>\n\t<li><tt>org.apache.commons.lang3.mutable.MutableInt</tt>: <b>30.6%</b></li>\n</ul>\n","customfield_10054":null,"fixVersions":null,"customfield_10055":null,"resolution":null,"customfield_10047":"13/Oct/23 11:07 AM","customfield_10048":null,"labels":null,"customfield_10049":null,"attachment":[{"self":"https://mojira.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/attachment/117535","id":"117535","filename":"crash-2023-10-13_18.43.29-server.txt","author":{"avatarUrls":{"48x48":"https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/default/default-avatar.png","24x24":"https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/default/default-avatar.png","16x16":"https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/default/default-avatar.png","32x32":"https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/default/default-avatar.png"},"displayName":"intsuc","active":true,"timeZone":"Asia/Tokyo","accountType":"customer"},"created":"13/Oct/23 3:05 AM","size":"2 kB","mimeType":"text/plain","content":"https://mojira.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/attachment/content/117535"},{"self":"https://mojira.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/attachment/117536","id":"117536","filename":"deobf_crash-2023-10-13_18.43.29-server.txt","author":{"avatarUrls":{"48x48":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/994aaa0b92148ffbc96e97271aa843ce?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FAB-5.png","24x24":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/994aaa0b92148ffbc96e97271aa843ce?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FAB-5.png","16x16":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/994aaa0b92148ffbc96e97271aa843ce?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FAB-5.png","32x32":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/994aaa0b92148ffbc96e97271aa843ce?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FAB-5.png"},"displayName":"Arisa Bot","active":true,"timeZone":"America/Los_Angeles","accountType":"atlassian"},"created":"13/Oct/23 3:05 AM","size":"2 kB","mimeType":"text/plain","content":"https://mojira.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/attachment/content/117536"},{"self":"https://mojira.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/attachment/117537","id":"117537","filename":"mc-265805.zip","author":{"avatarUrls":{"48x48":"https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/default/default-avatar.png","24x24":"https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/default/default-avatar.png","16x16":"https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/default/default-avatar.png","32x32":"https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/default/default-avatar.png"},"displayName":"intsuc","active":true,"timeZone":"Asia/Tokyo","accountType":"customer"},"created":"14/Oct/23 7:27 AM","size":"0.8 kB","mimeType":"application/zip","content":"https://mojira.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/attachment/content/117537"}],"versions":null,"resolutiondate":"30/Oct/23 2:25 AM","issuelinks":null,"updated":"25/Mar/25 12:25 PM","status":nu